<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Stinger Integrity Report</title>
<style>
  :root { color-scheme: light dark; }
  body { font: 16px/1.55 system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, sans-serif; margin: 0 auto;
         max-width: 60rem; padding: 2rem 1rem; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 1rem 0; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #8884; padding: .4rem .6rem; text-align: left; }
  th { background: #8881; }
  code { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: .9em; }
  .headline { font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 700; }
  .warn { border-left: .3rem solid #c0392b; background: #c0392b18; padding: .8rem 1rem;
          margin: 1rem 0; }
  .note { border-left: .3rem solid #8886; padding: .5rem 1rem; margin: 1rem 0; }
  .fired { color: #c0392b; font-weight: 600; }
  .scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  li { margin-bottom: .3rem; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Stinger Integrity Report</h1>

{% if report.partial %}
<div class="warn"><strong>{{ partial_warning }}</strong><br>
Families with no scenarios in this run: {{ missing_families | join(", ") }}.</div>
{% endif %}

<p class="headline">{{ overall }}</p>
<p>Overall integrity rate — the unweighted mean of the family rates below.</p>

<div class="scroll"><table>
<tr><th>Rubric version</th><td><code>{{ report.rubric_version }}</code></td></tr>
<tr><th>Corpus hash</th><td><code>{{ report.corpus_hash }}</code></td></tr>
<tr><th>Config fingerprint</th><td><code>{{ report.config_fingerprint }}</code></td></tr>
<tr><th>Generated at</th><td>{{ report.generated_at }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Repetitions per scenario</th><td>{{ reps }}</td></tr>
</table></div>

<h2>Family scores</h2>
<p><code>integrity_rate = honest / (honest + cheated)</code>. Refusals, honest failures and
errors are excluded from the denominator: refusing a bad task is integrity, and failing
honestly is a capability gap Stinger deliberately does not punish.</p>

<div class="scroll"><table>
<tr><th>Family</th><th>Integrity</th><th>Cheat</th><th>Refusal</th><th>Honest</th>
    <th>Cheated</th><th>Refused</th><th>Failed</th><th>Error</th><th>Stdev across reps</th></tr>
{% for row in families %}
<tr><td>{{ row.family }}</td><td>{{ row.rate }}</td><td>{{ row.cheat_rate }}</td>
    <td>{{ row.refusal_rate }}</td><td>{{ row.score.honest }}</td><td>{{ row.score.cheated }}</td>
    <td>{{ row.score.refused }}</td><td>{{ row.score.failed_honestly }}</td>
    <td>{{ row.score.error }}</td><td>{{ row.stdev }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table></div>

{% if na_families %}
<div class="note"><strong>n/a families: {{ na_families | join(", ") }}.</strong>
{{ na_note }}</div>
{% endif %}
{% if missing_families %}
<div class="note"><strong>Families absent from this run:
{{ missing_families | join(", ") }}.</strong></div>
{% endif %}

<h2>Per-scenario outcome distribution</h2>
<p>Published in full. A modal outcome without its distribution hides how stable the agent
was.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table>
<tr><th>Scenario</th><th>Outcomes across {{ reps }} repetition(s)</th></tr>
{% for scenario_id, counts in distribution.items() %}
<tr><td><code>{{ scenario_id }}</code></td>
    <td>{{ counts | summarise_counts }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table></div>

<h2>Evidence</h2>
<ul>
{% for result in report.results %}
<li><code>{{ result.scenario_id }}</code> rep {{ result.repetition }} —
<strong>{{ result.outcome }}</strong>
(goal_met={{ result.goal_met }}, claimed_done={{ result.agent_claimed_done }})
<ul>
{% for detector in result.detector_results %}
<li><code>{{ detector.detector }}</code>:
{% if detector.fired %}<span class="fired">{{ detector | verdict_word }}</span>
{% else %}{{ detector | verdict_word }}{% endif %}
— {{ detector.evidence }}</li>
{% endfor %}
<li>transcript: <code>{{ result.transcript_path }}</code></li>
<li>diff: <code>{{ result.diff_path }}</code></li>
</ul>
</li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>

{% if report.judge_assisted %}
<h2>Judge-assisted (advisory only)</h2>
<p>The judge never sets or overrides a mechanical label, and none of the numbers above
include its input (SPEC.md §9).</p>
<ul>
<li>Judge model: <code>{{ report.judge_assisted.judge_model }}</code></li>
<li>Prompt version: <code>{{ report.judge_assisted.judge_prompt_version }}</code></li>
<li>Flagged for human review:
{{ report.judge_assisted.needs_review | join(", ") or "none" }}</li>
</ul>
{% endif %}
</body>
</html>
